DATED                                                                                                           24, Jul, 2026
ETIHAD AIRWAYS PJSC
and
Trip Air Ticketing ( UK) Limited
PERFORMANCE AGREEMENT
Contract number: CT-037819
PERFORMANCE AGREEMENT
Effective Date: 01/04/2026 
PARTIES
(1)	ETIHAD AIRWAYS PJSC (a public joint stock company established by Emiri Decree No. 1 of 2003 in the Emirate of Abu Dhabi), whose principal place of business is at PO Box 35566, Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates  ("Etihad"); and
(2)	Trip Air Ticketing ( UK) Limited (incorporated and registered in London, United Kingdom, under company registration number 10811048, the registered office of which is at 10th Floor  70 St. Mary Axe, London, London, EC3A 8BE, GB   ("Agency"),
each, a “Party” and, collectively, the “Parties”.
RECITALS
WHEREAS Agency is in the business of providing travel related products and services and wishes to promote Etihad as one its preferred airlines on a non-exclusive basis;
WHEREAS Agency is appointed by Etihad under the terms of the Airline Reporting Corporation (“ARC”) Agent Reporting Agreement and/or the International Air Transport Association (“IATA”) Passenger Sales Agency Agreement (together the “Governing Agency Agreement”); and 
WHEREAS Etihad desires to make its products and services available for sale by Agency by incorporating the additional terms, protections, and conditions set forth in this Agreement.
WHEREAS The Parties may from time to time enter agreements referencing and supplemental to this Agreement setting out specific incentives and rewards for certain targets and activities (each a “Supplement”)
THEREFORE, in consideration and acknowledgment of the mutual promises and covenants contained in this Performance Agreement the Parties hereby agree as follows.
TERM and TERMINATION
The term of this Performance Agreement ("Agreement") shall commence on the 01-Apr-2026 and remain in effect until 30-Jun-2026 (the "Term") unless terminated earlier in accordance with the General Terms of Agreement as set out in Appendix A ("GTA") or as otherwise stipulated in the Agreement. For avoidance of doubt, Supplements shall have their own duration independent from the Agreement (the “Duration”).
Either Party may terminate this Agreement or any applicable Supplement(s) at any time and without cause by giving thirty (30) days' prior notice in writing to the other Party.
AGREEMENT
The Agreement incorporates the GTA, Supplement(s) and Appendices, which are attached to this Agreement, and sets out the whole agreement between the Parties and supersedes any previous arrangement, understanding or agreement (whether written or verbal) between Parties relating to the financial arrangements that are the subject matter of this Agreement. In addition, the Parties agree that they are bound by the Governing Agency Agreement.
Capitalized terms in the Agreement shall have the same meaning as in the relevant GTA, Supplement(s) and Appendices.
In the event of any inconsistency or a conflict in the terms and conditions of the main body of this Agreement, GTA, Supplements, the Appendices, and the terms and conditions of the attachments, the following order of precedence shall apply:
the Governing Agency Agreement, except as explicitly superseded by this Agreement;
the main body of this Agreement; 
the GTA;
the Supplements;
the Appendices (excluding the GTA in Appendix A).
AGENCY GROUP
Etihad and the Agency agree that in measuring performance against incentive targets each Supplement may include the performance by a member of the Agent’s group (including affiliates, franchisees, sales offices) as set in an annex to the relevant Supplement ("Agency Group"). Any payments under a Supplement shall only be made to the Agency and the account to out in Appendix B.
AGENCY'S OBLIGATIONS
The Agency agrees to:
comply with, and ensure that each member of the Agency Group complies with, the Governing Agency Agreement;
actively market and promote Etihad, identifying Etihad as a preferred airline for travel on all routes operated by Etihad;
use its best endeavours to ensure that each member of the Agency Group actively markets and promotes Etihad, identifying it as a preferred airline for travel on all routes operated by Etihad;
ensure that it has provided each member of the Agency Group with all sales, fare, product and promotional material/collateral or electronic communications, the links to or copies of the Policies required for the effective representation of Etihad services ;
ensure that all bookings (whether via GDS or any other relevant booking tool) are made to enable the tracking of all Etihad corporate contracts and their total travel volumes on Etihad (e.g. Other Service Information ("OSI") entries, corporate client code ("CCI") and business connect number, if applicable);
provide, upon request, Etihad with a monthly report of Etihad tickets sold by the Agency and each individual members of the Agency Group, broken down by ticket class and route;
use any in-house databases to communicate details of Etihad promotions, products and services to all relevant employees of the Agency and (where relevant) to all relevant employees of the Agency Group;
use its best endeavours to provide each passenger's mobile number and email address (but no less than at least 50%) of bookings from the Agency. Agency must obtain the passenger's consent to the disclosure of such information so that Etihad may contact the passenger in case of operational issues such as flight cancellation, schedule or equipment changes, overbooking or for product/service support. If the passenger declines to provide information, this must be clearly indicated in the booking remarks;
provide to Etihad a local point of contact and provide access to the locations covered in this Agreement;
